<h2>Similarities</h2>

<div class="section">
<h3>1. Salvation Through Faith Alone</h3>

<p>
Martin Luther believed that salvation is through faith alone, known as <strong>sola fide</strong>.
</p>

<p class="quote">
“The just shall live by faith” (Romans 1:17).
</p>

<p>
This belief continues in South Miami Lutheran Church today by emphasizing God’s grace and faith in Jesus Christ for salvation.
</p>
</div>


<div class="section">
<h3>2. The Bible as the Highest Authority</h3>

<p>
Another similarity between Martin Luther and South Miami Lutheran Church is the belief that the Bible is the highest authority in Christianity, also called <strong>sola scriptura</strong>.
</p>

<p class="quote">
“A simple layman armed with Scripture is greater than the mightiest pope without it” (Luther).
</p>

<p>
The church follows this idea through Bible readings and sermons based on Scripture during worship services.
</p>
</div>


<div class="section">
<h3>3. The Priesthood of All Believers</h3>

<p>
Luther believed that all Christians can have a direct relationship with God without needing a priest to communicate with God on their behalf.
</p>

<p class="quote">
“All Christians are truly of the spiritual estate” (Luther).
</p>

<p>
This idea is shown in South Miami Lutheran Church through encouraging members to participate in worship, Bible studies, and church activities.
</p>
</div>


